{{also|copout|cop-out}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from {{m|en|cop a plea}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-cop out.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[avoid]] or [[shirk]], either by failing to perform, or by performing in a grossly [[insufficient]], [[negligent]], or [[superficial]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|Faced with the prospect of cooking for himself, his first thought was to '''cop out''' and order a pizza.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2000|author=Bill Oddie|authorlink=Bill Oddie|title=Gripping Yarns|page=67|passage=There was no bird fair at Druridge so I didn't have to feel guilty about '''copping out''' of it.}}
# To [[plead]] [[guilty]] and ask for [[mercy]].

====Synonyms====
* [[weasel out]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|cop-out}}

